msgid "A biome whose sounds were not loaded yet starts its day or night ambience by the time of day. The game plays the opposite one (night sounds by day) until the next biome or day change."
msgstr "A biome whose sounds were not hauled yet starts its sunrise or dark watch ambience by th' time o' sunrise. Th' voyage plays th' opposite one (dark watch sounds by sunrise) until th' next biome or sunrise change, arr!"

msgid "A blow that destroys a character's head cuts it off, by the same rule the Dismemberment setting cuts off limbs. In the game a destroyed head only kills."
msgstr "A blow that destroys a character's head cuts it off, by th' same rule th' Dismemberment settin' cuts off limbs. In th' voyage a destroyed head only kills, arr!"

msgid "A character knocked down or killed by a blow falls with its own momentum and is pushed away from the hit, harder the heavier the blow and most at the part that was struck, its arms and legs flung by it, and a cut-off head flies the same way. Limp bodies have joints that ease to a stop and a slight muscle tone, so they settle into natural poses. In the game a body drops where it stood, its joints stopping hard."
msgstr "A sea dog knocked down or killed by a blow falls wi' its own momentum an' be pushed away from th' hit, harder th' heavier th' blow an' most at th' part that was struck, its arms an' legs flung by it, an' a cut-off head flies th' same way. Limp bodies have joints that ease t' a avast an' a slight muscle tone, so they settle into natural poses. In th' voyage a body drops where it stood, its joints stoppin' hard, arr!"

msgid "A character on a bench with the table behind it sits facing away from the table. The game mirrors the bench's look point through the middle of the world map, so the sitter faces an unrelated direction."
msgstr "A sea dog on a bench wi' th' table behind it sits facin' away from th' table. Th' voyage mirrors th' bench's spy point through th' middle o' th' seven seas chart, so th' sitter faces an unrelated direction, arr!"

msgid "A character that takes a fatal hit explodes, covers everything around in blood and sends bones flying everywhere. Its gear falls to the ground around the spot."
msgstr "A sea dog that takes a fatal hit explodes, covers everythin' around in blood an' sends bones flyin' everywhere. Its gear falls t' th' ground around th' spot, arr!"

msgid "A character that turned its head toward what it was talking to or watching looks ahead again once it stops looking. In the game the head stays turned until the next thing it looks at."
msgstr "A sea dog that turned its head toward what it was talkin' t' or watchin' looks ahead again once it stops lookin'. In th' voyage th' head stays turned until th' next thin' it looks at, arr!"

msgid "A character's bag window opens with their inventory until you close it with OPEN BAG. In the game every bag stays shut after loading until OPEN BAG is pressed for it."
msgstr "A character's bag window opens wi' their inventory until ye batten down it wi' OPEN BAG. In th' voyage every bag stays shut after haulin' until OPEN BAG be pressed fer it, arr!"

msgid "A click on a stack picks up all of it, Shift+click half, Ctrl+click one item, and Shift+Ctrl+click asks how many with a slider. In the game a click picks up one item and Shift or Ctrl the whole stack."
msgstr "A click on a stack picks up all o' it, Shift+click half, Ctrl+click one booty, an' Shift+Ctrl+click asks how many wi' a slider. In th' voyage a click picks up one booty an' Shift or Ctrl th' whole stack, arr!"

msgid "A double click on a squad member far from the view (or a double tap of their number) flies the camera there in an arc instead of cutting."
msgstr "A double click on a crew hand far from th' view (or a double tap o' their number) flies th' camera thar in an arc instead o' cuttin', arr!"

