msgid "stores the game's 3D models more compactly, so they take about half the video memory and look practically the same; in detail, the game's meshes store most corners once for every triangle that uses them, each copy with its own triangle's tangent; Meitou merges the copies that differ only in that tangent into one vertex with their averaged tangent, so meshes keep about 60% fewer vertices (object meshes at The Hub take 50 MB of video memory instead of 98) and the bump lighting barely changes (tangents move 4° on average); applies to meshes loaded after the change (docs/render-objects.md)"
msgstr "stores th' game's 3D models more compactly, so they take about half th' video memory an' spy practically th' same; in detail, th' game's meshes store most corners once fer every triangle that uses them, each copy wi' its own triangle's tangent; Meitou merges th' copies that differ only in that tangent into one vertex wi' their averaged tangent, so meshes keep about 60% fewer vertices (object meshes at Th' Hub take 50 MB o' video memory instead o' 98) an' th' bump lightin' barely changes (tangents move 4° on average); applies t' meshes hauled after th' change (docs/render-objects.md)"

